    skos:prefLabel "Schwarzfigurig"@de,
        "Black-figure"@en .

th:concept_e87c9480 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader th:concept_778bbb97 ;
    skos:definition "Refers to a style of Greek vase painting that developed from the Black-figure style. It appeared in Athens around 530 BCE and spread to other areas of Greece, southern Italy, Etruria, and elsewhere in the Mediterranean area, until it disappeared in the third century BCE. The style is characterized by a particular technique, which involves the use of refined slip and a two-phase firing process to create a black ground through sintering, with figures reserved in red. The details of the figures are more fluid than in the Black-figure style, and are typically drawn with a brush, using both a defined, black relief line and a more dilute line that varies in color from dark gold to black."@en ;
    skos:inScheme th:scheme ;
    skos:narrower th:concept_000479cb,
